    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0378" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg264"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811b.01/63</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Committee on Insular Affairs of
                        the House of Representatives</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fairfield</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March 25,
                        1924</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: The Insular Affairs Committee of the
                    House of Representatives has directed me to inquire of the State Department as
                    to whether the granting of Independence at this time to the <pb facs="0379"
                        n="265" xml:id="pg265"/> Philippine Islands would be contrary to any
                    provisions of the Four Power Pact.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d215-f1"/></p>
                <p>An early reply would be very much appreciated.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis W.
                    Fairfield</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
